C52.8 79.1 53 75.9 52.4 75.6C50.8 74.7 51.3 72.2 53.2 71.9C55.3 71.5 56.4 74.6 54.5 75.6C54.3 75.7 54.3 75.7 54.3 76.1C54.3 77.5 54 79.7 53.6 81.3C53.5 82.1 53.4 82.1 53.9 82C59.9 80.7 63.2 74.1 60.4 68.6C58.7 65 54.9 62.9 51 63.3Z"></path></svg>
<span style="font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.04em">osewa</span>
</a>
<nav aria-label="Main" style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 0 24px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px">
<a href="#why" style="text-decoration: none; padding: 12px 0">why</a>
<a href="#bench" style="text-decoration: none; padding: 12px 0">benchmarks</a>
<a href="#start" style="text-decoration: none; padding: 12px 0">quick start</a>
<a href="#roadmap" style="text-decoration: none; padding: 12px 0">roadmap</a>
<a href="#how" style="text-decoration: none; padding: 12px 0">how it works</a>
<a href="#agents" style="text-decoration: none; padding: 12px 0">agents</a>
<a href="https://github.com/rjyo/osewa" style="text-decoration: none; padding: 12px 0">github ↗</a>
</nav>
</div>
</header>

<section style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 72px 24px 64px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 48px">
<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; gap: 8px 24px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; color: #5B5B57; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em">
<span>Wire protocol v0 · open source</span><span>QUIC / UDP 7322 · TLS WebSocket / TCP 7322</span>
</div>
<h1 style="margin: 0; font-size: clamp(48px, 8vw, 100px); line-height: 0.95; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.05em; max-width: 1050px">The terminal protocol that never drops<span style="color: #E0393E">.</span></h1>
<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 40px; align-items: stretch; border-top: 1px solid #111111; padding-top: 32px">
<div style="flex: 1 1 380px; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 28px">
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.5; color: #2A2A28">Like ssh, but the session survives the network. Like mosh, but it forwards ports, runs commands and works where UDP is blocked.</p>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; color: #4A4A46">osewa runs your remote shell over QUIC when UDP gets through and TLS WebSocket when it doesn't. The session lives on the host, not in the connection, so a dead link is just a reconnect.</p>
<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px">
<a href="#start" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; min-height: 52px; padding: 0 24px; background: #111111; color: #F4F4F1; font-weight: 600; font-size: 16px; text-decoration: none">Get started <span style="color: #FF6A4D">→</span></a>
<a href="https://github.com/rjyo/osewa" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 52px; padding: 0 24px; border: 1px solid #111111; color: #111111; font-weight: 500; font-size: 16px; text-decoration: none">Star on GitHub</a>
<a href="#bench" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 52px; padding: 0 8px; color: #111111; font-weight: 500; font-size: 16px">Benchmarks</a>
</div>
</div>

<div role="img" aria-label="Shell history: ssh in 1995, mosh in 2012, osewa in 2026" style="flex: 1 1 520px; min-width: 0; background: #111111; color: #F4F4F1; padding: 32px 36px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: clamp(16px, 1.6vw, 20px); line-height: 1.9; overflow-x: auto">
<div class="hl0"><span style="color: #FF8A73">$</span> <span class="ty" style="display: inline-block; overflow: hidden; vertical-align: bottom">history</span><span class="ty-cur" style="display: inline-block; width: 0.55em; height: 1.05em; background: #FF6A4D; vertical-align: -0.18em"></span></div>
<div class="hl hl1" style="color: #5E5E59">  1995  ssh devbox</div>
<div class="hl hl2" style="color: #8C8C86">  2012  mosh devbox</div>
<div class="hl hl3" style="color: #F4F4F1">  2026  osewa attach devbox</div>
<div class="hl hl4"><span style="color: #FF8A73">$</span> <span class="pulse" style="display: inline-block; width: 0.55em; height: 1.05em; background: #FF6A4D; vertical-align: -0.18em"></span></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section aria-label="Headline numbers" style="border-top: 1px solid #111111; border-bottom: 1px solid #111111; background: #FFFFFF">
<div style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr))">
<div style="padding: 28px 24px; border-right: 1px solid #D3D3CE; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<div style="font-size: 52px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.04em; line-height: 1">12<span style="font-size: 28px">×</span></div>
<div style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.45; color: #4A4A46">faster key echo than ssh during a download on cellular</div>
</div>
<div style="padding: 28px 24px; border-right: 1px solid #D3D3CE; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<div style="font-size: 52px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.04em; line-height: 1">0.4<span style="font-size: 28px"> s</span></div>
<div style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.45; color: #4A4A46">to resume after sleep or an IP change (mosh 1.1 s, ssh dies)</div>
</div>
<div style="padding: 28px 24px; border-right: 1px solid #D3D3CE; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<div style="font-size: 52px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.04em; line-height: 1">4<span style="font-size: 28px">×</span></div>
<div style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.45; color: #4A4A46">faster than ssh to connect and run a command, Thailand → Tokyo</div>
</div>
<div style="padding: 28px 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<div style="font-size: 52px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.04em; line-height: 1">14.3<span style="font-size: 28px"> MB</span></div>
<div style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.45; color: #4A4A46">memory per idle session on the host, half of ssh's</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section id="why">
<div style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 88px 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 48px">
<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px 56px; align-items: baseline">
<div style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: #B8262C">§1 Why now</div>
<h2 style="flex: 1 1 520px; margin: 0; font-size: clamp(34px, 4.5vw, 52px); line-height: 1.02; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.04em">ssh and mosh were built for networks we no longer have.</h2>
</div>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; color: #2A2A28; max-width: 820px">Bandwidth is no longer the hard part. Soon almost anywhere will have at least Starlink, and even that carries tens of Mbit/s. What hurts now is latency, deep buffers, switching networks and blocked UDP. And on the other end there's often a coding agent, redrawing a full-screen TUI for hours while you check in from a laptop or a phone.</p>

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); border-top: 1px solid #111111">
<div style="padding: 24px 24px 28px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; border-right: 1px solid #D3D3CE">
<div style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between"><span style="font-size: 26px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.03em">ssh</span><span style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: #5B5B57">1995</span></div>
<div style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.5; color: #2A2A28">Built for one steady wired link. The session is its TCP connection, so it dies when the network changes, and under load each key waits behind the download.</div>
</div>
<div style="padding: 24px 24px 28px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; border-right: 1px solid #D3D3CE">
<div style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between"><span style="font-size: 26px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.03em">mosh</span><span style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: #5B5B57">2012</span></div>
<div style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.5; color: #2A2A28">Bet on saving scarce bandwidth with its own emulator. When that emulator reads output differently from your terminal you get garbled text, and it's UDP only, with no forwards and no scrollback.</div>
</div>
<div style="padding: 24px 24px 28px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; background: #111111; color: #F4F4F1">
<div style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between"><span style="font-size: 26px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.03em">osewa</span><span style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: #FF8A73">2026</span></div>
<div style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.5; color: #E4E4DF">Built for plenty of bandwidth with bad latency and queues. The session lives on the host with Ghostty's terminal engine, and forwards and exec share the same connection, over QUIC or TCP.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div style="overflow-x: auto; border-top: 1px solid #111111">
<table style="width: 100%; min-width: 760px; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 15px">
<caption style="text-align: left; padding: 14px 0; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: #5B5B57">Side by side</caption>
<thead><tr style="text-align: left; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; color: #5B5B57">
<th scope="col" style="padding: 12px 16px 12px 0; font-weight: 400; border-bottom: 1px solid #111111; width: 22%"></th>
<th scope="col" style="padding: 12px 16px; font-weight: 400; border-bottom: 1px solid #111111">ssh</th>
<th scope="col" style="padding: 12px 16px; font-weight: 400; border-bottom: 1px solid #111111">mosh</th>
<th scope="col" style="padding: 12px 16px; font-weight: 600; border-bottom: 1px solid #111111; color: #111111; background: #FFFFFF">osewa</th>
</tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><th scope="row" style="text-align: left; padding: 14px 16px 14px 0; font-weight: 500; border-bottom: 1px solid #D3D3CE">Session</th><td style="padding: 14px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid #D3D3CE; color: #4A4A46">Dies with the TCP connection</td><td style="padding: 14px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid #D3D3CE; color: #4A4A46">Survives roaming</td><td style="padding: 14px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid #D3D3CE; background: #FFFFFF">Lives on the host: survives roaming, sleep and server restarts</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row" style="text-align: left; padding: 14px 16px 14px 0; font-weight: 500; border-bottom: 1px solid #D3D3CE">Transport</th><td style="padding: 14px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid #D3D3CE; color: #4A4A46">TCP</td><td style="padding: 14px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid #D3D3CE; color: #4A4A46">UDP only</td><td style="padding: 14px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid #D3D3CE; background: #FFFFFF">QUIC, falling back to TLS over TCP</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row" style="text-align: left; padding: 14px 16px 14px 0; font-weight: 500; border-bottom: 1px solid #D3D3CE">Screen on the host</th><td style="padding: 14px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid #D3D3CE; color: #4A4A46">None, bytes are replayed</td><td style="padding: 14px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid #D3D3CE; color: #4A4A46">Its own emulator, no scrollback</td><td style="padding: 14px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid #D3D3CE; background: #FFFFFF">libghostty-vt, Ghostty's terminal engine</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row" style="text-align: left; padding: 14px 16px 14px 0; font-weight: 500; border-bottom: 1px solid #D3D3CE">Beyond the shell</th><td style="padding: 14px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid #D3D3CE; color: #4A4A46">Port forwards, exec</td><td style="padding: 14px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid #D3D3CE; color: #4A4A46">Terminal only</td><td style="padding: 14px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid #D3D3CE; background: #FFFFFF">Port forwards and exec on the same connection</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row" style="text-align: left; padding: 14px 16px 14px 0; font-weight: 500; border-bottom: 1px solid #D3D3CE">Kitty protocols</th><td style="padding: 14px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid #D3D3CE; color: #4A4A46">Passed through</td><td style="padding: 14px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid #D3D3CE; color: #4A4A46">No</td><td style="padding: 14px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid #D3D3CE; background: #FFFFFF">Keyboard; graphics with animation, kept on the host and redrawn on reconnect; clipboard reads and paste events</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row" style="text-align: left; padding: 14px 16px 14px 0; font-weight: 500; border-bottom: 1px solid #111111">Modern OSC</th><td style="padding: 14px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid #111111; color: #4A4A46">Passed through</td><td style="padding: 14px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid #111111; color: #4A4A46">Few</td><td style="padding: 14px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid #111111; background: #FFFFFF">Yes: hyperlinks, cwd, prompt marks, agent status (OSC 7501)</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section id="bench" style="border-top: 1px solid #111111; background: #FFFFFF">
<div style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 88px 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 64px">
<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px 56px; align-items: baseline">
<div style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: #B8262C">§2 Benchmarks</div>
<h2 style="flex: 1 1 520px; margin: 0; font-size: clamp(34px, 4.5vw, 52px); line-height: 1.02; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.04em">On a bad network, keys echo 8–100× faster than ssh.</h2>
</div>

<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px">
<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; align-items: baseline">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 22px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em">Key echo while a download runs on the same connection</h3>
<div style="display: flex; gap: 18px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; color: #4A4A46">
<span style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px"><span style="width: 12px; height: 12px; background: #E0393E"></span>osewa · best</span>
<span style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px"><span style="width: 12px; height: 12px; background: #8F8F89"></span>ssh</span>
</div>
</div>
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 22px">
{echoRows.map((r) => (<Fragment>
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(150px, 220px) minmax(0, 1fr) 64px; gap: 8px 20px; align-items: center">
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px"><span style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: 500">{r.name}</span><span style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; color: #5B5B57">{r.cond}</span></div>
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px">
<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px" title={`osewa ${r.o}`}><div class="grow" style={`height: 18px; width: ${r.ow}; min-width: 4px; background: #E0393E; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0`}></div><span style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; white-space: nowrap">{r.o}</span></div>
<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px" title={`ssh ${r.s}`}><div class="grow" style={`height: 18px; width: ${r.sw}; background: ${r.sFill}; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0`}></div><span style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; white-space: nowrap; color: #4A4A46">{r.s}</span></div>
</div>
<div style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 18px; font-weight: 500; color: #B8262C; text-align: right">{r.x}</div>
</div>
</Fragment>))}
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(150px, 220px) minmax(0, 1fr) 64px; gap: 20px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; color: #5B5B57">
<span></span>
<div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; border-top: 1px solid #D3D3CE; padding-top: 6px"><span>0</span><span>500</span><span>1,000</span><span>1,500</span><span>2,000 ms</span></div>
<span></span>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 500px), 1fr)); gap: 48px">

<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px">
<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; gap: 10px; align-items: baseline">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 22px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em">Back after an IP change</h3>
<button type="button" data-replay style="min-height: 44px; padding: 0 14px; border: 1px solid #111111; background: #FFFFFF; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; cursor: pointer">↻ replay in real time</button>
</div>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5; color: #4A4A46">Client moved to a new IP after 5 s offline. Time from the network coming back to a working session.</p>
<div id="replay-bars" style="display: contents">
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px">
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 64px minmax(0, 1fr) 72px; gap: 12px; align-items: center"><span>osewa</span><div style="height: 18px; background: #F4F4F1"><div class="rt-o" style="height: 18px; width: 20%; background: #E0393E; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0"></div></div><span>0.4 s</span></div>
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 64px minmax(0, 1fr) 72px; gap: 12px; align-items: center"><span>mosh</span><div style="height: 18px; background: #F4F4F1"><div class="rt-m" style="height: 18px; width: 55%; background: #8F8F89; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0"></div></div><span>1.1 s</span></div>
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 64px minmax(0, 1fr) 72px; gap: 12px; align-items: center"><span>ssh</span><div style="height: 18px; background: #F4F4F1; display: flex; align-items: center"><div class="rt-s" style="height: 18px; width: 6%; background: #8F8F89"></div><span class="rt-x" style="margin-left: 8px; color: #B8262C">✕ session gone</span></div><span style="color: #B8262C">never</span></div>
</div>
</div>
