<section aria-labelledby="res-h" style="border-bottom: 1px solid #111111">
<div style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 88px 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 40px">
<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px 56px; align-items: baseline">
<div style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: #B8262C">§4 Resource use</div>
<div style="flex: 1 1 520px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
<h2 id="res-h" style="margin: 0; font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 44px); line-height: 1.05; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.04em">Light when idle. Honest about the cost.</h2>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; color: #4A4A46">osewa keeps the real screen, so it parses everything the program writes, where ssh just forwards bytes. That's host CPU on heavy output, and it's why a flood can't slow your program down.</p>
