<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 260px), 1fr)); gap: 32px">
{resources.map((m) => (<Fragment>
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; border-top: 2px solid #111111; padding-top: 14px">
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px"><span style="font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600">{m.title}</span><span style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; color: #5B5B57">{m.note}</span></div>
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px">
{m.rows.map((r) => (<Fragment>
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 48px minmax(0, 1fr) 70px; gap: 8px; align-items: center"><span>{r.n}</span><div style="height: 14px"><div class="grow" style={`height: 14px; width: ${r.w}; min-width: 3px; background: ${r.fill}; border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0`}></div></div><span style="text-align: right">{r.v}</span></div>
</Fragment>))}
</div>
</div>
</Fragment>))}
</div>
<p style="margin: 0; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6; color: #5B5B57; max-width: 900px">Same container and run as the lab benchmarks, osewa over TLS WebSocket. An idle session uses under 0.1% CPU on both ends for all three. In a flood the program wrote 173 MB/s under osewa, 22 MB/s under mosh and 1.2 MB/s under ssh.</p>
</div>
</section>

<section id="start" style="background: #FFFFFF; border-bottom: 1px solid #111111">
<div style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 88px 24px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 40px">
<div style="flex: 1 1 340px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px">
<div style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: #B8262C">§5 Quick start</div>
<h2 style="margin: 0; font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 44px); line-height: 1.05; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.04em">ssh once. osewa after that.</h2>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.6; color: #4A4A46">osewa login uses ssh one time to install itself on the host and enroll your device with an Ed25519 key. From then on it runs on its own port, and even updates go over osewa. Linux and macOS hosts.</p>
</div>
<div style="flex: 1 1 560px; min-width: 0; background: #111111; color: #E9E9E4; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.9; padding: 24px 28px; overflow-x: auto; white-space: pre">
<div><span style="color: #FF8A73">$</span> osewa login --service me@devbox   <span style="color: #8C8C86"># install, enroll, run as a user service</span></div>
<div><span style="color: #FF8A73">$</span> osewa attach devbox               <span style="color: #8C8C86"># attach to (or create) a session</span></div>
<div><span style="color: #FF8A73">$</span> osewa forward devbox 3000         <span style="color: #8C8C86"># forward localhost:3000</span></div>
<div><span style="color: #FF8A73">$</span> osewa exec devbox -- make test    <span style="color: #8C8C86"># run a command, no terminal</span></div>
<div><span style="color: #FF8A73">$</span> osewa update devbox               <span style="color: #8C8C86"># upgrade the host over osewa</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section id="roadmap" aria-labelledby="road-h">
<div style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 88px 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 40px">
<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px 56px; align-items: baseline">
<div style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: #B8262C">§6 Roadmap</div>
<h2 id="road-h" style="flex: 1 1 520px; margin: 0; font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 44px); line-height: 1.05; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.04em">A transport any terminal can ride, then a mux on top.</h2>
</div>
<div style="overflow-x: auto; padding-bottom: 4px">
<div style="min-width: 1100px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(7, minmax(0, 1fr)); column-gap: 0; row-gap: 18px">
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; padding-right: 20px">
<div style="position: relative; height: 30px"><div class="grow" style="position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: 13px; height: 4px; background: #111111; animation-delay: 0.0s"></div><div style="position: relative; width: 30px; height: 30px; border-radius: 50%; background: #111111; color: #F4F4F1; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 14px">✓</div></div>
<div style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px">M0 · <span style="color: #4A4A46">shipped</span></div>
<strong style="font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -0.01em">Wire protocol v0</strong>
<span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5; color: #4A4A46">An open contract for frames, sessions and channels, in docs/PROTOCOL.md.</span>
</div>
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; padding-right: 20px">
<div style="position: relative; height: 30px"><div class="grow" style="position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: 13px; height: 4px; background: #111111; animation-delay: 0.2s"></div><div style="position: relative; width: 30px; height: 30px; border-radius: 50%; background: #111111; color: #F4F4F1; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 14px">✓</div></div>
<div style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px">M1 · <span style="color: #4A4A46">shipped</span></div>
<strong style="font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -0.01em">Sessions that survive</strong>
<span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5; color: #4A4A46">QUIC with TLS WebSocket fallback, sessions held on the host, exactly-once input, keystrokes ahead of bulk, the latest screen on a slow link.</span>
</div>
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; padding-right: 20px">
<div style="position: relative; height: 30px"><div class="grow" style="position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: 13px; height: 4px; background: #111111; animation-delay: 0.5s"></div><div style="position: relative; width: 30px; height: 30px; border-radius: 50%; background: #111111; color: #F4F4F1; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 14px">✓</div></div>
<div style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px">M2 · <span style="color: #4A4A46">shipped</span></div>
<strong style="font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -0.01em">Agent-aware</strong>
<span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5; color: #4A4A46">Status from the agent (OSC 7501), colour queries answered on the host, kitty keys and graphics.</span>
</div>
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; padding-right: 20px">
<div style="position: relative; height: 30px"><div style="position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: 14px; height: 2px; background: repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, #5B5B57 0 6px, transparent 6px 12px)"></div><div class="grow" style="position: absolute; left: 0; width: 15px; top: 13px; height: 4px; background: #111111; animation-delay: .75s"></div><div style="position: relative; width: 30px; height: 30px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center"><div class="pulse" style="position: absolute; inset: 0; border-radius: 50%; background: #E0393E; opacity: .3"></div><div style="width: 16px; height: 16px; border-radius: 50%; background: #E0393E; box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px #F4F4F1"></div></div></div>
<div style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px">M3 · <span style="color: #B8262C; font-weight: 600">release · you are here</span></div>
<strong style="font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -0.01em">Release: the osewa CLI</strong>
<span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5; color: #4A4A46">One binary for macOS and Linux. <code style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px">osewa login</code> once over ssh, then attach, forward, exec and update over osewa.</span>
</div>
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; padding-right: 20px">
<div style="position: relative; height: 30px"><div style="position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: 14px; height: 2px; background: repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, #A9A9A2 0 6px, transparent 6px 12px)"></div><div style="position: relative; width: 30px; height: 30px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center"><div style="width: 16px; height: 16px; border-radius: 50%; border: 2px solid #5B5B57; background: #F4F4F1; box-sizing: border-box"></div></div></div>
<div style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px">M4 · <span style="color: #111111; font-weight: 600">next</span></div>
<strong style="font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -0.01em">In the Moshi app</strong>
<span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5; color: #4A4A46">osewa as a transport in Moshi on iOS and Android, beside mosh. The first app to ride it: resume, forwarding, and no UDP needed.</span>
</div>
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; padding-right: 20px">
<div style="position: relative; height: 30px"><div style="position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: 14px; height: 2px; background: repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, #A9A9A2 0 6px, transparent 6px 12px)"></div><div style="position: relative; width: 30px; height: 30px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center"><div style="width: 16px; height: 16px; border-radius: 50%; border: 2px solid #5B5B57; background: #F4F4F1; box-sizing: border-box"></div></div></div>
<div style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px">M5 · <span style="color: #5B5B57">later</span></div>
<strong style="font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -0.01em">Mux</strong>
<span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5; color: #4A4A46">Tabs, splits and workspaces held on the host, like tmux. Every pane is its own session with its own flow control.</span>
</div>
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; padding-right: 20px">
<div style="position: relative; height: 30px"><div style="position: absolute; left: 0; width: 15px; top: 14px; height: 2px; background: repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, #A9A9A2 0 6px, transparent 6px 12px)"></div><div style="position: relative; width: 30px; height: 30px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center"><div style="width: 16px; height: 16px; border-radius: 50%; border: 2px solid #5B5B57; background: #F4F4F1; box-sizing: border-box"></div></div></div>
<div style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px">M6 · <span style="color: #5B5B57">later</span></div>
<strong style="font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -0.01em">Every screen</strong>
<span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5; color: #4A4A46">A terminal, a desktop app or a phone attaches to the same layout. One terminal engine between you and the program.</span>
</div>
<div style="grid-column: 1 / span 5; margin-right: 12px; background: #111111; color: #F4F4F1; padding: 12px 16px; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px"><strong style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 16px">Transport</strong><span style="color: #FF8A73">usable on its own, today</span></div>
<div style="grid-column: 6 / span 2; border: 1px dashed #5B5B57; padding: 11px 16px; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px"><strong style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 16px">Mux</strong><span style="color: #5B5B57">one client of the same protocol</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section id="how" style="border-top: 1px solid #111111">
<div style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 88px 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 56px">
<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px 56px; align-items: baseline">
<div style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: #B8262C">§7 How it works</div>
<h2 style="flex: 1 1 520px; margin: 0; font-size: clamp(34px, 4.5vw, 52px); line-height: 1.02; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.04em">Separate the session from the transport. Then make the transport hard to kill.</h2>
</div>

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 520px), 1fr)); gap: 24px">

<div style="background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #D3D3CE; padding: 28px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px">
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
<div style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; color: #5B5B57">01 · hybrid carrier</div>
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 24px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em">QUIC and TLS WebSocket, raced on every connect</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.55; color: #4A4A46">The same frames run on both. QUIC gets a 300 ms head start; if UDP is blocked, the WebSocket wins. Nothing to configure.</p>
</div>
<div role="group" aria-label="Network" style="display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap">
<button type="button" class="tg" data-set="udp:open" aria-pressed="true" style="min-height: 44px; padding: 0 16px; border: 1px solid #111111; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; cursor: pointer">UDP open</button>
<button type="button" class="tg" data-set="udp:blocked" aria-pressed="false" style="min-height: 44px; padding: 0 16px; border: 1px solid #111111; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; cursor: pointer">UDP blocked</button>
</div>
<div style="display: flex; align-items: stretch; gap: 14px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px">
<div style="flex: 0 0 72px; border: 1px solid #111111; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; text-align: center; padding: 8px">client</div>
<div style="flex: 1 1 auto; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; gap: 26px; min-width: 0">
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 8px"><span>QUIC · UDP</span><span style="color: #5B5B57">1 RTT</span></div>
<div style="position: relative; height: 14px">
<div style="position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: 6px; height: 2px; background: #D3D3CE"></div>
<div data-when="udp:open" style="display: contents"><div class="q-go" style="position: absolute; top: 0; width: 14px; height: 14px; border-radius: 50%; background: #E0393E"></div></div>
<div data-when="udp:blocked" hidden style="display: contents"><div class="q-stall" style="position: absolute; top: 0; width: 14px; height: 14px; border-radius: 50%; background: #E0393E"></div><div class="x-in" style="position: absolute; left: calc(38% + 20px); top: -4px; font-size: 16px; color: #B8262C">✕ dropped</div></div>
</div>
</div>
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 8px"><span>TLS WebSocket · TCP</span><span style="color: #5B5B57">+300 ms</span></div>
<div style="position: relative; height: 14px">
<div style="position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: 6px; height: 2px; background: #D3D3CE"></div>
<div class="w-go" style="position: absolute; top: 0; width: 14px; height: 14px; border-radius: 50%; background: #55554F"></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div style="flex: 0 0 72px; border: 1px solid #111111; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; text-align: center; padding: 8px">host</div>
</div>
<div style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; padding: 12px 14px; background: #F4F4F1"><span data-when="udp:open">connected over QUIC in one round trip</span><span data-when="udp:blocked" hidden>UDP blocked → connected over TLS WebSocket, +300 ms</span></div>
</div>

<div style="background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #D3D3CE; padding: 28px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px">
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px">
<div style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; color: #5B5B57">02 · the host keeps the real screen</div>
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 24px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em">Connections come and go. The session stays.</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.55; color: #4A4A46">Each terminal runs in its own process on the host and keeps the exact screen with libghostty-vt. Reconnecting sends one snapshot, not a replay. Pings spot a dead path in about a second, and unacked keys are resent.</p>
</div>
<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; padding: 12px 0">
<div style="flex: 0 0 120px; border: 1px solid #111111; padding: 12px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; position: relative; min-height: 64px">
<span>laptop</span>
<span class="cyc1" style="position: absolute; left: 12px; top: 34px; color: #5B5B57">wi-fi</span>
<span class="cyc2" style="position: absolute; left: 12px; top: 34px; color: #B8262C">asleep</span>
<span class="cyc3" style="position: absolute; left: 12px; top: 34px; color: #5B5B57">5G</span>
</div>
<div style="flex: 1 1 auto; position: relative; height: 40px; min-width: 60px">
<div class="lnk" style="position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: 19px; height: 2px; background: #111111"></div>
<span class="cyc2" style="position: absolute; left: 50%; top: -2px; transform: translateX(-50%); color: #B8262C; white-space: nowrap">link lost</span>
<span class="cyc3" style="position: absolute; left: 50%; top: -2px; transform: translateX(-50%); color: #5B5B57; white-space: nowrap">resumed 0.4 s</span>
</div>
<div style="flex: 0 0 170px; background: #111111; color: #F4F4F1; padding: 12px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<span>host · session</span>
<span style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; color: #9FE0A8"><span class="pulse" style="width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; background: #9FE0A8"></span>PTY alive</span>
<span style="color: #C9C9C2">screen kept · 0 keys lost</span>
</div>
</div>
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1px; background: #D3D3CE; border: 1px solid #D3D3CE; font-size: 13px; text-align: center">
<div style="background: #FFFFFF; padding: 12px 8px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px"><strong style="font-size: 18px">~1 s</strong><span style="color: #5B5B57">dead path detected</span></div>
<div style="background: #FFFFFF; padding: 12px 8px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px"><strong style="font-size: 18px">500 ms</strong><span style="color: #5B5B57">between redial races</span></div>
<div style="background: #FFFFFF; padding: 12px 8px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px"><strong style="font-size: 18px">exactly once</strong><span style="color: #5B5B57">every keystroke</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div style="background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #D3D3CE; padding: 28px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; grid-column: 1 / -1">
<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px 40px; align-items: flex-end; justify-content: space-between">
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; max-width: 640px">
<div style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; color: #5B5B57">03 · keystrokes first</div>
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 24px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em">A download can't bury your echo</h3>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.55; color: #4A4A46">Frames go out by priority: control, terminals, exec, then forwards. While you type, bulk is held to the path's bandwidth-delay product plus 40 ms of queue. Each forward gets its own QUIC stream, so a lost packet in a download never blocks a key.</p>
</div>
<div role="group" aria-label="Protocol" style="display: flex; gap: 8px">
<button type="button" class="tg" data-set="mode:ssh" aria-pressed="true" style="min-height: 44px; padding: 0 16px; border: 1px solid #111111; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; cursor: pointer">ssh</button>
<button type="button" class="tg" data-set="mode:osewa" aria-pressed="false" style="min-height: 44px; padding: 0 16px; border: 1px solid #111111; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; cursor: pointer">osewa</button>
</div>
</div>
<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 20px">
<div style="flex: 1 1 520px; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px">
<div data-when="mode:osewa" hidden style="display: contents">
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px">
<span style="color: #5B5B57">terminal stream · priority</span>
<div style="position: relative; height: 26px; border: 1px solid #111111; overflow: hidden">
<div class="key-fast" style="position: absolute; top: 3px; width: 18px; height: 18px; background: #E0393E; color: #FFFFFF; font-size: 11px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center">k</div>
</div>
</div>
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px">
<span style="color: #5B5B57">download · its own stream, capped at BDP + 40 ms</span>
<div style="position: relative; height: 26px; border: 1px solid #111111; overflow: hidden">
<div class="flow" style="position: absolute; top: 3px; left: 0; width: 200%; display: flex; gap: 10px">
<span style="flex: 0 0 36px; height: 18px; background: #A9A9A2"></span><span style="flex: 0 0 36px; height: 18px; background: #A9A9A2"></span><span style="flex: 0 0 36px; height: 18px; background: #A9A9A2"></span><span style="flex: 0 0 36px; height: 18px; background: #A9A9A2"></span><span style="flex: 0 0 36px; height: 18px; background: #A9A9A2"></span><span style="flex: 0 0 36px; height: 18px; background: #A9A9A2"></span><span style="flex: 0 0 36px; height: 18px; background: #A9A9A2"></span><span style="flex: 0 0 36px; height: 18px; background: #A9A9A2"></span><span style="flex: 0 0 36px; height: 18px; background: #A9A9A2"></span><span style="flex: 0 0 36px; height: 18px; background: #A9A9A2"></span><span style="flex: 0 0 36px; height: 18px; background: #A9A9A2"></span><span style="flex: 0 0 36px; height: 18px; background: #A9A9A2"></span>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div data-when="mode:ssh" style="display: contents">
<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px">
<span style="color: #5B5B57">one TCP stream · keys queue behind the download</span>
<div style="position: relative; height: 26px; border: 1px solid #111111; overflow: hidden">
<div class="flow" style="position: absolute; top: 3px; left: 0; width: 200%; display: flex; gap: 4px">
