<section id="agents" aria-labelledby="agents-h" style="border-top: 1px solid #111111; background: #FFFFFF">
<div style="max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 88px 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 48px">
<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px 56px; align-items: baseline">
<div style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; color: #B8262C">§8 Built for agents</div>
<h2 id="agents-h" style="flex: 1 1 520px; margin: 0; font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 44px); line-height: 1.05; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.04em">The agent keeps working. You check in when it needs you.</h2>
</div>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; color: #2A2A28; max-width: 860px">A coding agent runs for hours in a full-screen TUI, and you check in from wherever you are. osewa keeps that screen on the host in libghostty-vt, so what the agent's terminal does reaches you whole on every reconnect. The host answers the agent's queries itself, so it never waits on a client that's asleep.</p>

<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 500px), 1fr)); gap: 32px">

<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em">Status, from the agent to you (OSC 7501)</h3>
<div style="background: #111111; color: #E9E9E4; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.8; padding: 18px 20px; overflow-x: auto; white-space: pre">
<div><span style="color: #FF8A73">$</span> osewa ls devbox</div>
<div style="color: #8C8C86">ID     TITLE         IDLE  STATUS</div>
<div style="position: relative">api    claude-code   2h    <span class="ag1" style="position: absolute; color: #E9E9E4">working 40%</span><span class="ag2" style="position: absolute; color: #FF8A73">blocked: permission — Apply?</span><span class="ag3" style="position: absolute; color: #9FE0A8">done</span>&nbsp;</div>
<div>web    codex         14m   working</div>
<div>logs   tail -f       3d    -</div>
</div>
<p style="margin: 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.55; color: #4A4A46">osewa keeps each session's status on the host. When you attach, a blocked or done agent shows a one-line notice. A new prompt (OSC 133) ends a working or blocked status.</p>
</div>

<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em">What the agent's output may do</h3>
<div style="border: 1px solid #111111; padding: 18px 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px">
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 64px minmax(0, 1fr) 96px; gap: 10px; color: #5B5B57"><span>agent</span><span style="text-align: center">host</span><span style="text-align: right">your terminal</span></div>

<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 64px minmax(0, 1fr) 96px; gap: 10px; align-items: center">
<span style="font-weight: 600; color: #111111">reaches</span>
<div style="position: relative; height: 12px"><div style="position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: 5px; height: 2px; background: #111111"></div><div style="position: absolute; left: 50%; top: -2px; width: 2px; height: 16px; background: #5B5B57"></div><div class="ln-pass" style="position: absolute; top: 0; width: 12px; height: 12px; border-radius: 50%; background: #E0393E"></div></div>
<span style="text-align: right">✓ drawn</span>
</div>
<div style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; color: #4A4A46">Prompt marks, links, titles, current directory, pointer shape, notifications (live only), clipboard copies, kitty keys, kitty graphics and kitty paste events.</div>
</div>

<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 64px minmax(0, 1fr) 96px; gap: 10px; align-items: center">
<span style="font-weight: 600; color: #111111">answered</span>
<div style="position: relative; height: 12px"><div style="position: absolute; left: 0; width: 50%; top: 5px; height: 2px; background: #111111"></div><div style="position: absolute; left: 50%; right: 0; top: 5px; height: 2px; background: repeating-linear-gradient(90deg, #A9A9A2 0 4px, transparent 4px 8px)"></div><div style="position: absolute; left: 50%; top: -2px; width: 2px; height: 16px; background: #5B5B57"></div><div class="ln-ans" style="position: absolute; top: 0; width: 12px; height: 12px; border-radius: 50%; background: #E0393E"></div></div>
<span style="text-align: right; color: #5B5B57">asleep is fine</span>
</div>
<div style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; color: #4A4A46">Colour and light/dark queries are answered on the host, from your terminal's last known colours. Status is kept there too.</div>
</div>

<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px">
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 64px minmax(0, 1fr) 96px; gap: 10px; align-items: center">
<span style="font-weight: 600; color: #111111">dropped</span>
<div style="position: relative; height: 12px"><div style="position: absolute; left: 0; width: 50%; top: 5px; height: 2px; background: #111111"></div><div style="position: absolute; left: 50%; top: -2px; width: 2px; height: 16px; background: #5B5B57"></div><div class="ln-drop" style="position: absolute; top: 0; width: 12px; height: 12px; border-radius: 50%; background: #55554F"></div></div>
<span style="text-align: right; color: #B8262C">✕ never sent</span>
</div>
<div style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; color: #4A4A46">Other OSCs, DCS (including tmux passthrough), APC, PM and SOS. Clipboard reads need <code style="font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px">--clipboard-read</code>, and only the owner gets them.</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
<h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em">Every sequence: what mosh and osewa do with it</h3>
